{'name': 'Navat Capital Management LLC', 'city': 'Bet Shemesh', 'country': 'Israel', 'location': {'lat': 31.7542644, 'lon': 34.9962552}, 'description': 'The Navat Fund is a fundamental Long/Short equity strategy with low net market exposure principally focused on Small and Mid-Cap companies operating in the Semiconductor, Energy Transition Materials and Industrial Technology sectors. The strategy primarily trades in Europe and the UK, and opportunistically in global developed markets.

Navat is managed by Toby Kram who has over 20 years’ buy-side investment experience, most recently as Partner and Sector Head at Eisenstat Capital Partners.

Toby is supported by Rory Pike, Head of Research.'}

strategy_description:
MW Alpha Plus Fund is a global, multi-asset, market neutral Fund, run predominantly on a systematic basis. It aims to generate a consistent absolute
return with low correlation to equities and a volatility target range of 6-10%*. The Fund seeks to capitalise on over a decade of quantitative research,
data gathering, and cutting-edge trade execution infrastructure.

management_company:
{'name': 'Balyasny Asset Management', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.76387, 'lon': -73.9723575}, 'description': 'Balyasny Asset Management L.P. (“BAM” or the “Management Company” or the “Firm”) is a global institutional investment firm dedicated to delivering consistent, uncorrelated absolute returns in all market environments. BAM is headquartered in Chicago, with offices globally. The firm was founded in 2001 by Dmitry Balyasny, Managing Partner & Chief Investment Officer, Taylor O’Malley, Co-Founding Partner & Chairman, and Scott Schroeder, Co-Founding Partner.

The Fund started with an Equities Long/Short strategy and has developed over time into a multi-strategy, multi-PM model, which reflects a blend of strategies including Equities Long/Short, Fixed Income & Macro, Commodities, Multi-Asset Arbitrage, and Systematic investing. 

Our objective is to generate uncorrelated alpha for our partners through diversified strategies and strong risk management. Each PM team is given the autonomy, within a defined risk framework, to deploy capital in its respective discipline dependent upon market conditions. We rely on constant innovation, and we will continue to evolve our investment process to meet the demands of the ever-changing market. We also seek to add value via PM & team development, trading & execution, research, and data & technology.'}

{'name': 'Interval Partners', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.757372, 'lon': -73.9715061}, 'description': 'Interval Partners, LP (“Interval”) is an alternative investment firm focused on generating uncorrelated alpha through diversified standalone investment strategies. 

We specialize in sector-focused, fundamental equity long/short low-net strategies, utilizing a bottom-up investment approach with active portfolio and risk management. Our robust institutional infrastructure supports each investment strategy, allowing individual portfolio managers to preside over their own business and focus 100% of their time on stewarding client capital. We manage pooled investment vehicles and separately managed accounts in partnership with our clients to achieve their investment objectives.

Based in New York, NY, Interval was founded in March 2012 by Gregg Moskowitz, Connor McLaughlin, and Ray Fernandez.  Our portfolio managers and their associated strategies include: Gregg Moskowitz (Consumer/Industrials/Tech), Connor McLaughlin (Tech), Anil Stevens (Financials), Elise Crumbine (Consumer Discretionary), Ned Gilliss (Cyclicals), and Jeff Schleppy (Energy & Power).'}

