{'name': 'Bracebridge Capital, LLC', 'city': 'Boston', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 42.3475062, 'lon': -71.08393029999999}, 'description': 'Bracebridge Capital, LLC (“Bracebridge” or the “firm”) is a leading alternative asset manager founded in 1994 by Nancy Zimmerman and Gabriel Sunshine. The firm has approximately 175 employees, including about 80 investment and quantitative research professionals. The senior investment team of 8 principals is highly stable, with an average tenure of more than 20 years working together.

The investment objective of Bracebridge is to achieve absolute returns and capital preservation by identifying and capitalizing on inefficiencies in global financial markets. We believe markets are inefficient, and the absolute return funds seek to capture the cheapness or richness created by these inefficiencies while hedging risks related to interest rates, foreign exchange, and credit. By seeking to hedge these macro risks, the funds’ strategy is focused on isolating the source of potential excess returns and creating a portfolio with a return profile that is intended to be largely uncorrelated with systemic factors. 

Bracebridge is selectively open to a small number of new partners to raise $1-2 billion of capital.'}

{'name': 'Bayforest Technologies', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4988194, 'lon': -0.1333026}, 'description': 'Prior to founding Bayforest in 2017 Dr. Theodoros Tsagaris was central to the development of Tudor’s London quantitative proprietary trading desk over 6.5 years and one of the few PMs to run partner money as well as client money.

Bayforest uses machine learning and big data techniques where appropriate to the investment process.  This is an advancement on Theo’s academic work at Imperial (PhD and published papers).  This academic sophistication is combined with his practical experience of building and trading investment strategies across multiple asset classes and investment products since 2004 at Bluecrest, GSA and Tudor.

Bayforest has a multi-disciplinary team with an average of circa 20 years domain expertise per employee combining institutional software product development with data science and trading experience.  It is this combination of disciplines we feel is central to the firm’s success.'}

{'name': 'BFAM Partners', 'city': 'Hong Kong', 'country': 'Hong Kong SAR', 'location': {'lat': 22.2865106, 'lon': 114.1916401}, 'description': 'BFAM Partners is an Asia Pacific focused multi-strategy Fund with dynamic asset allocation amongst Credit, Equity Linked, and Volatility Arbitrage strategies

Benjamin A. Fuchs, Chief Investment Officer, has run this group of strategies since 2007 and has 31 years experience in Asian markets with a focus on Asian markets. We endeavor to run dynamic capital allocation amongst strategies. Returns driven by short term tactical trading and medium-term positioning

BFAM currently has 26 full time employees (12 investment professionals + 14 non-investment professionals) and is headquartered in Hong Kong'}

{'name': 'Chenavari Financial Group Ltd', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4970873, 'lon': -0.1395648}, 'description': "Chenavari is an established, credit-focused asset manager with a core expertise in European markets. With expertise across the liquidity spectrum of credit, Chenavari aims to profit from idiosyncrasies and inefficiencies within credit markets, which are due to macro (such as banks' deleveraging, monetary policies, etc.) as well as technical factors. The Firm concentrates its investment activity on fundamental strategies that may offer attractive risk-reward profiles on a relative value basis with low market correlation and low beta to broad credit markets.

Chenavari’s investment strategies can be segmented across three groups: 

•	Liquid strategies, including investments in single name corporates, European financials, credit indices, asset-backed securities, across both cash and derivative markets;
•	Private Credit strategies, such as portfolio acquisitions of primarily performing loans; risk sharing/significant risk transfer, asset-based lending, and specialty finance (new loan origination) in consumer finance, receivables and leasing; and
•	CLO management, including investment in senior secured loans and revolving credit facilities through European collateralised loan obligation structures."}

{'name': 'Carrhae Capital LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5088023, 'lon': -0.1351061}, 'description': 'Carrhae Capital is an alpha-focused global emerging markets equity manager, founded by Ali Akay in 2011 following a decade-long career as a portfolio manager at SAC, HBK, and Goldman Sachs Principal Strategies. The firm is headquartered in London and employs a team of 24 professionals with research team members present on-the-ground in Brazil, China, India and the UAE. 
 
Carrhae manages US$ 3 billion across two very distinct strategies (Long-Short Absolute Return and Long Only Emerging Markets), utilizing a unified investment process, research engine, and team. The Long-Short strategy launched in December 2011 and aims to generate absolute returns, while the Long-Only strategy launched in February 2014 and seeks to achieve alpha above the Emerging Markets Index. 
 
Carrhae Capital LLP is regulated by the FCA and registered with the SEC. Carrhae Capital (DIFC) Limited is regulated by the DFSA.'}

{'name': 'LFIS Capital', 'city': 'Paris', 'country': 'France', 'location': {'lat': 48.8421379, 'lon': 2.3219514}, 'description': 'LFIS Capital (LFIS) is a quantitative asset manager headquartered in Paris, France. 
LFIS was established in 2013, and is a partner of Walter GAM since 2021.

Employing 35 professionals with extensive Asset Management, capital markets and derivatives experience, LFIS manages assets for institutional clients and has expertise in traditional factors, implied parameters, synthetic credit, mid-frequency statistical arbitrage and hedging strategies.'}

{'name': 'Linear B Partners LP', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7516293, 'lon': -73.9754935}, 'description': 'Linear B Partners is a specialist relative value credit manager investing in global developed corporate and structured credit markets.

The flagship fund employs a market-neutral and absolute return strategy targeting consistent risk adjusted returns over a market cycle with no correlation to global credit and equity risk indices.

Linear B Partners was founded in 2021 by Michio Brunner and Patrick Gresens. The senior leadership have over 43 years of combined experience trading and structuring credit transactions at JPMorgan and at Palm Lane Credit Opportunities (fka JPS), working together since 2005.'}

