{'name': 'Svelland Capital', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4975884, 'lon': -0.1426189}, 'description': 'Svelland Capital, founded in 2016 by Tor Andre Svelland, is a commodities and freight-focused investment firm managing approximately USD 1bn. Tor brings over 30 years of commodity and shipping market experience from Trafigura, Goldman Sachs, Carnegie, and Klaveness. The firm’s flagship Svelland Global Trading Fund (launched 2017) employs a discretionary, trading-oriented long/short strategy across energy, metals, and freight markets, delivering returns with low correlation to equity and credit markets. The strategy expresses risk through a blend of commodity and freight derivatives and related equities. Svelland also manages the Svelland Commodities Futures Plus strategy, a discretionary L/S futures-only strategy with a 3-year track record, accessed via SMA and benefiting from low margin requirements. In addition, the firm co-owns and manages a physical gold ETC in partnership with Edmond de Rothschild. 

Svelland Capital (Cayman) Ltd is the manager (the “Manager”) of Svelland Global Trading Master Fund (the “Fund”) and has appointed Mirabella Financial Services LLP as the AIFM of the Fund. 

Svelland Capital (UK) Ltd is a wholly owned entity of Svelland Capital (Cayman) Ltd and is an Appointed Representative of Mirabella Advisers LLP, which is authorised and regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority.'}

