{'name': 'Fortlake Asset Management', 'city': 'Sydney', 'country': 'Australia', 'location': {'lat': -33.8653767, 'lon': 151.2100187}, 'description': 'Fortlake Asset Management was established in late 2020 and founded by Dr Christian Baylis, who managed $10 billion at UBS and worked at the Reserve Bank of Australia before that. 

Fortlake is a global absolute return fixed income specialist. Fortlake uses a variety of silos to add value and reduce correlations to traditional asset classes, utilising its capability within the fixed income market. Fortlake is also regarded as a specialist in the default arbitrage market – a negative correlation market that actively harvests defaults across High yield and Investment grade markets in the US and Europe. 
 
Fortlake sets strategic priorities across its portfolios and reflects these via active tilts across the relevant silos in order to manage correlations and risk.  Fortlake then undertakes a detailed review of implementation strategies to make sure that risk is managed in a way that is commensurate with the Fund risk and return objectives. Each silo has its own factors and quantitative research process. The process seeks an optimal balance between risk and return using the silos as levers. Therefore the investment team’s main function is to constantly review the ex-ante risk environment, maintain balance with the silos/levers and update implementation, so as to maintain an optimal ex-ante portfolio.'}

{'name': 'Cheyne Capital Management (UK) LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5042596, 'lon': -0.1398612}, 'description': "Cheyne Capital was founded in 2000 by Jonathan Lourie (CEO) and Stuart Fiertz (President) after working together at Morgan Stanley. 

Cheyne is one of Europe's leading alternative investment fund managers (AIFMs) with c. 170 partners and employees.

Cheyne invests across the capital structure from the senior debt to the equity of corporates and real estate. With an investment philosophy grounded in rigorous fundamental analysis, the firm’s main areas of expertise are: Real Estate Debt, Corporate Credit and Risk Transfer, European Strategic Value Credit, and Liquid Alternatives."}

strategy_description:
Manteio GALIS Fund is a mix of data-driven strategies and thesis-driven liquid strategies, marrying Manteio's proprietary trading background and experience with data driven AI methodologies. Currently, Manteio GALIS Fund consists of four strategy verticals:

1) Equity Statistical Arbitrage, consisting of data-driven approaches that leverage either an investment thesis or Artificial Intelligence methodologies; 

2) Equity Market Liquidity, consisting of trading-oriented liquid strategies which seek to identify short-term dislocations and demand for liquidity in equity markets; 

3) Quantitative Fixed Income, consisting of both statistical and liquidity-providing trading strategies generally focused on sovereign rates; and 

4) Systematic Futures and FX, consisting of data-driven high turnover strategies seeking to exploit short and medium-term dislocations across asset classes.

Manteio GALIS Master Fund LP was launched October 1, 2021 with a subset of current GALIS strategies. Manteio GALIS Fund changed its investment mandate to the four strategy verticals as of December 2024. A detailed schedule of Manteio GALIS Master Fund LP's full track record is available upon request.

management_company:
{'name': 'Marek Capital', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7515507, 'lon': -73.97892209999999}, 'description': 'Marek Capital is an alternative investment manager that looks beyond surface-level econometrics, delving deep into the inner workings of the financial system and consumer behavior to uncover overlooked opportunities. 

Marek specializes in thematic and relative value multi-strategy investing across mortgages, rates, structured credit, corporate credit, and related equities within a rigorous risk framework. 

Marek Capital is co-founded by Matthew Cherwin, former Chief Investment Officer and Treasurer of JP Morgan, and Derek Goodman, former Managing Partner of Autonomy Capital.'}

{'name': 'Third Point LLC', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7553714, 'lon': -74.0014842}, 'description': 'Third Point (the "Firm") is an institutional investment manager based in New York City that employs an event-driven, opportunistic approach to invest globally across the capital structure and in diversified asset classes to optimize risk-reward through market cycles.

Our platform is rooted across three key asset frameworks: [1] Equities (Fundamental, Event-Driven, Activism), [2] Credit (Corporate & Sovereign Credit, Structured Credit), and [3] Private Investing (Private Credit, Insurance Solutions, and Venture Capital).

The Firm is driven by an ethos of continuous self and organizational improvement, a desire to embrace change and evolution, and a commitment to putting our investors first. Led by founder Daniel S. Loeb, the Firm has a 70-person investment team, a quantitative data and analytics team, as well as a dedicated business team. Third Point manages assets for sovereign wealth funds, endowments, foundations, corporate & public pensions, high-net-worth individuals, and employees.'}

{'name': 'Dendur Capital LP', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7649432, 'lon': -73.98308589999999}, 'description': 'Dendur is an event-driven hedge fund whose strategy combines deep fundamental research with rigorous event analysis applied through a market lens.  Dendur invests across the capital structure with an orientation towards midcap equities and manages a concentrated portfolio of longs and shorts built around idiosyncratic situations.  The fund employs a flexible approach, investing across asset classes, event types and market cycles, allowing the team to find the most attractive investment opportunities in a given market environment.

Dendur was founded by Malcolm (Mac) Levine who brings over a decade of investing experience from his role as Director of Research at Corvex Management and as a Principal in Private Equity at Apollo Management LP.  Along with Mr. Levine, the other members of Dendur’s investment team have experience investing in public and private markets across various strategies, which creates a differentiated perspective in event investing. 

Mr. Levine invested the majority of his liquid net worth in the Dendur funds directly alongside investors.  In addition, the firm has a strategic relationship with a premier day-one institutional investor.'}

{'name': 'Divisadero Street Capital', 'city': 'Miami', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 25.7266961, 'lon': -80.2441987}, 'description': 'Divisadero Street Partners, LP is a Miami-based hedge fund launched in October 2021. The firm employs a long/short equity strategy with a small-and-mid-cap focus and low net exposure, aiming to compound and protect capital in all market conditions. The catalyst-driven research process, rooted in fundamental  analysis, identifies both long and short opportunities with a focus on asymmetric risk/reward.

Led by William Zolezzi, CFA, with 10+ year buyside experience, the fund takes an active short-selling approach, viewing its short book as a profit center rather than a hedge.  

A substantial portion of the PM’s net worth is invested in the fund, reinforcing alignment with investors.'}

{'name': 'Burkehill Global Management', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7576743, 'lon': -73.9762354}, 'description': "Burkehill employs a global equity event-driven investment strategy and strives to achieve consistent, uncorrelated high-quality returns by leveraging robust fundamental analysis, disciplined process, and prudent risk management. Burkehill is active in 45 global markets, and generates alpha via opportunities across assets, sectors and products.

The firm was formed in July 2021, and its first fund was launched in January 2022 with the backing of a pedigreed anchor Investor. Burkehill expanded in early 2024, successfully achieving its targeted fundraising goal from a select group of synergistic investors.

Burkehill's senior team-which has an average 17+ years of industry experience-has deep fundamental investment expertise across products and geographies, and throughout the corporate lifecycle, spanning global public equities, as well as select private and debt opportunities."}

{'name': 'Anson Advisors Inc.', 'city': 'Toronto', 'country': 'Canada', 'location': {'lat': 43.6472617, 'lon': -79.3785998}, 'description': 'Anson Funds is a privately held alternative asset management company founded in 2003, with offices in Toronto, Canada and Dallas, Texas.

Anson Funds invests primarily in publicly-traded equity and debt securities on a global basis.

We prioritize net of fees performance with low volatility of returns and low correlations to broad market indexes.'}

{'name': 'Sternlight Capital Partners LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.51273699999999, 'lon': -0.1553055}, 'description': 'Sternlight generates alpha through a repeatable process targeting asymmetric, catalyst-driven long and short opportunities in European credit. The strategy is run by a team with decades of fundamental investment experience and is well positioned to capitalize on the growing market dislocations across the liquid European credit universe.  

The team is led by Stefan Tsonev (CIO) who has over 27 years of investment experience, most recently as a senior portfolio manager for the flagship, multi-billion dollar credit hedge funds at PIMCO, in London.

The Firm began deploying the strategy in September 2023 in a managed account format - if interested, please get in touch and we would be happy to discuss the strategy and returns.'}

{'name': 'Astaris Capital Management LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5072313, 'lon': -0.1514495}, 'description': "Founded in 2019, Astaris Capital Management is an opportunistic, event driven credit and equities fund manager which seeks to benefit from identifying debt and equity valuation dislocations among select European names where there is a catalyst to monetise that dislocation.

The firm's CIO, Martin Beck, has over two decades of event driven investing experience, including 8 years as founding partner at Sothic Capital. The team has been working together for multiple years, combining over five decades of relevant investing experience.

Astaris launched the Astaris Special Situations Master Fund in February of 2020, seeded by former investors and the CIO's former line manager."}

