{'name': 'Deltroit Asset Management (UK) LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5058664, 'lon': -0.1369406}, 'description': 'Deltroit is a London based alternative investment firm managing assets for institutional investors, private banks and individuals. 

Lord Hintze founded Deltroit Asset Management to continue the management of his long-standing Directional Opportunities Fund, established in 2005. At Deltroit Asset Management, Lord Hintze and his team manage research-driven credit strategies through a bottom-up fundamental approach, supplemented and balanced by top-down geopolitical and macro analysis. This process also provides for thematic investments across adjacent global markets, to build a multi-asset investment portfolio to further supplement returns. 

Deltroit Asset Management (UK) LLP (“Deltroit”) is a limited liability partnership incorporated in England and Wales under partnership number OC448813, and with its registered office at 1st Floor, 50 Pall Mall, London, United Kingdom, SW1Y 5JH. Deltroit is authorised and regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority (FRN: 1020296).'}

{'name': 'Etna Capital Management', 'city': 'Hong Kong', 'country': 'Hong Kong SAR', 'location': {'lat': 22.2815571, 'lon': 114.1584036}, 'description': "Etna Capital is an asset management company founded by ex-Sequoia China professionals. Etna Capital has established a comprehensive range of AI-themed investment products, including venture funds, a public equity hedge fund and a NASDAQ-listed ETF. The AUM of all investment vehicles is over 1 billion USD.

Over the years, we've developed insights into and established connections within global technology companies. Through fundamental-driven and AI-empowered investment processes, we aim to capture long-term and high-growth AI-related opportunities. Since 2011, we have established significant exposure in major AI-native companies globally.

For the public equity hedge fund, we combine private equity-style in-depth due diligence and public equity risk-reward philosophies. We aim to capture long-term alpha for investors while controlling risks."}

{'name': 'Cheyne Capital Management (UK) LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5042596, 'lon': -0.1398612}, 'description': "Cheyne Capital was founded in 2000 by Jonathan Lourie (CEO) and Stuart Fiertz (President) after working together at Morgan Stanley. 

