Although convertible securities remain a primary focus, Silverback has also found increasing success and opportunities throughout the capital structure. Silverback continues to view the convertible market as one of the best markets for capitalizing on significant market dislocations that may occur, and it is likely that Silverback may meaningfully allocate the Fund’s capital to convertible investments if and when dislocations occur. In general, Silverback uses convertibles in various ways, which depends on the market cycle and security life cycle."}

strategy_description:
The investment objective of the Fund is to generate absolute investment returns by primarily investing (whether directly or indirectly) in listed and unlisted equities and equities-derivatives, convertible bonds, government bonds in the following markets:
i. India;
ii. South Asia excluding India;
iii. United States (including American Depository Receipts ("ADRs");
iv. Japan; and
v. Such other markets as the Manager may determine from time to time.

management_company:
{'name': 'Lingotto', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5148368, 'lon': -0.1571998}, 'description': 'Established in 2023, Lingotto exists to deliver attractive long-term returns to its limited partners.‍ We will achieve this by constantly challenging conventional thinking to create something exceptional for the long term. We openly acknowledge that Lingotto is not the right home for everybody. It’s a home for those willing and able to embrace the extraordinary.

At Lingotto, we have assembled a unique team of outstanding investment professionals who can express themselves in order to generate outperformance for our clients. At Lingotto they are free to pursue their passion for investing without the bureaucracy of most large organisations, or the loneliness of standalone funds.

We have multiple investment strategies, each led by a Managing Partner and Chief Investment Officer (CIO). The unifying thread is a commitment to being curious, courageous, humble and patient. Where appropriate we are comfortable with concentration, illiquidity and volatility, which we view as opportunities rather than risks.'}

{'name': 'CIBRA Capital', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4935249, 'lon': -0.2263414}, 'description': 'CIBRA Capital is a UK investment management firm founded by Cristian Cibrario in 2023. The firm manages an event-driven and risk arbitrage strategy, investing primarily in announced corporate transactions alongside a broader set of event-related opportunities. 

CIBRA is led by an experienced team with backgrounds in investment banking and law with particular expertise in global regulatory and antitrust processes. 

CIBRA’s opportunity set is equity-focused, global, and agnostic to sector and market cap, resulting in a diversified and market-neutral portfolio.'}

{'name': 'Jerpoint Capital (UK) Management Ltd', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5086448, 'lon': -0.1432729}, 'description': 'Jerpoint Capital is a global investment management firm founded by Seán Murphy, formerly a Portfolio Manager at Citadel.

Jerpoint continues the global event-driven equity strategy Seán led at Citadel, combining risk arbitrage with fundamental equity investing. In risk arbitrage, we focus on announced M&A situations, while in fundamental equities we construct a beta- and factor-neutral portfolio of compounding businesses where strategic change can unlock value.

Our disciplined, process-driven approach, rigorous portfolio construction, and focus on risk management are designed to deliver strong absolute and risk-adjusted returns across market cycles.'}

{'name': 'Cadian Capital Management, LP', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7604559, 'lon': -73.97342929999999}, 'description': 'Cadian Capital Management is an investment manager, founded by Eric Bannasch in October 2007. The Firm launched with its flagship fund, Cadian Fund, a long/short equity strategy concentrated in companies <$25 billion in market capitalization. This fund is focused on the technology, media, and telecommunications sectors, with additional exposure to consumer, healthcare, industrials, and related sectors.

In August 2022, the Firm launched Cadian Opportunities Fund, a best ideas strategy that is concentrated on select long positions derived from the flagship fund. 

The Firm has a sophisticated investor base, most of whom have been with us for more than 10 years. The Founder and senior professionals have significant investments in the funds, approximately 12% of AUM.  The Firm has a single New York City office with 21 employees.'}

{'name': 'Anson Advisors Inc.', 'city': 'Toronto', 'country': 'Canada', 'location': {'lat': 43.6472617, 'lon': -79.3785998}, 'description': 'Anson Funds is a privately held alternative asset management company founded in 2003, with offices in Toronto, Canada and Dallas, Texas.

Anson Funds invests primarily in publicly-traded equity and debt securities on a global basis.

We prioritize net of fees performance with low volatility of returns and low correlations to broad market indexes.'}

{'name': 'Spring Investments', 'city': 'Geneva', 'country': 'Switzerland', 'location': {'lat': 46.2024085, 'lon': 6.1578039}, 'description': 'Spring Investments SA is a wealth and asset management company based in Geneva, Switzerland. The Company commenced its wealth management operations in 2018 by Mr. Guy Avneon. The Company is authorized and regulated by FINMA .

 The Company offers discretionary portfolio management services and acts as the investment manager for Spring Subordinated Debt Fund, a Cayman Islands-domiciled fund launched in February 2020. 

The Company is highly experienced in fixed income investment strategies and also offers special mandate investment solutions for corporates, high net worth individuals, and family office clients.'}

{'name': 'Ruffer LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4970873, 'lon': -0.1395648}, 'description': "Founded in 1994, Ruffer is an independent, owner-managed, London based investment firm with $23bn of assets under management. Led by our founder and Chairman, Jonathan Ruffer, and co-CIOs, Henry Maxey and Neil McLeish, we have a team of over 300 employees and provide an investment service to pension funds, endowments and foundations, family offices and other institutions globally. 

We have a single global, macro-driven, absolute return investment strategy. Our aim is to deliver positive returns in all market environments, with a particular focus on downside protection in times of market stress. The entirety of the firm's AUM is managed this way. For over 30 years, our approach has been successful in delivering returns with a low correlation to equities and other asset classes. 

This is the result of an investment philosophy grounded in capital preservation, and a disciplined and genuinely different process. We conduct our own independent research, actively manage the underlying securities and operate freely, without the constraint of market benchmarks."}

{'name': 'Cheyne Capital Management (UK) LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5042596, 'lon': -0.1398612}, 'description': "Cheyne Capital was founded in 2000 by Jonathan Lourie (CEO) and Stuart Fiertz (President) after working together at Morgan Stanley. 

Cheyne is one of Europe's leading alternative investment fund managers (AIFMs) with c. 170 partners and employees.

Cheyne invests across the capital structure from the senior debt to the equity of corporates and real estate. With an investment philosophy grounded in rigorous fundamental analysis, the firm’s main areas of expertise are: Real Estate Debt, Corporate Credit and Risk Transfer, European Strategic Value Credit, and Liquid Alternatives."}

