{'name': 'Energy Group Capital LLC', 'city': 'Houston', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 29.7564216, 'lon': -95.49620829999999}, 'description': 'Energy Group Capital - Geoff Karren (ex-Passport Capital/ex-Pelorus Jack Capital). Market- and beta-neutral, high idio, low volatility and uncorrelated strategy focused on the energy transition. 

Our portfolio spans traditional and emerging energy sectors, as well as energy-adjacent industries, with an emphasis on uncorrelated returns and low volatility. 

Fundamental, bottoms up investors. PM has a well-established reputation for successful shorting, alpha generation and a deep energy sector background. Fund aims to produce uncorrelated, excellent risk-adjusted returns. GP committing majority of his liquid net worth to the fund, at least $8 million. Morgan Stanley and JP Morgan are intended to be prime brokers, MSFS is intended to be fund admin. Initial launch Launched in late 2024. Based in Austin, Texas, and San Francisco, California USA'}

{'name': 'Meridian & Saturn Capital Pte. Ltd. (MS Capital)', 'city': 'Singapore', 'country': 'Singapore', 'location': {'lat': 1.2988407, 'lon': 103.7878988}, 'description': 'Meridian & Saturn Capital Pte. Ltd. ( “MS Capital” ) was founded in Singapore by our CIO Jiaqi Zhu (Jude) and CEO Kate Zhang in 2022, as an important footstep for international expansion of Meridian China. It is registered under Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) for Fund Management business since November 2023.

Founded in October 2013 in China, Meridian Global Inc. established itself as market-leading China A-share high frequency trading firm and one of the earliest China manager to adopt deep learning into the quantitative investment process since 2016. 

Globally the group manages around $800mil USD across different quantitative strategies such as Equities Market Neutral (China-A, Pan-Europe, Japan), Enhanced Indexing/Long-only (China-A), Systematic macro (Global) and Convertible Bond (China). We have 80+ talented employees across research, portfolio management, infrastructure, operations and other business functions.'}

{'name': 'Silver Point Capital LP', 'city': 'Greenwich', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 41.02091619999999, 'lon': -73.62497309999999}, 'description': 'Silver Point Capital, L.P. (“Silver Point”, the “Firm”, "we") was founded in 2002 by Edward Mulé and Robert O’Shea, both previously partners at Goldman Sachs (“Goldman”), where together they built and co-headed numerous global credit businesses for the firm. 

Upon departing from Goldman, Mr. Mulé and Mr. O’Shea partnered to establish Silver Point in 2002 to replicate the credit businesses that they had built and managed while at Goldman. The Founders’ vision for Silver Point was to build a world-class private investment firm that would specialize in investing in credit and special situations opportunities.  They believed that they could leverage their experience and expertise to build a global credit investing business that would seek to generate attractive risk-adjusted returns across credit cycles for its investors.

Today, the Firm manages approximately $45 billion in investable assets across synergistic credit strategies, comprising (1) opportunistic credit and special situations funds, which include an evergreen global special situations investing strategy focused on publicly traded credit markets (the “Flagship Hedge Funds”) managing $13 billion in investable assets, (2) a dislocation drawdown strategy (the “Dislocation Drawdown Funds”) managing $7 billion in investable assets,  (3) a performing middle market lending strategy (our “Direct Lending Strategy”) managing $17 billion in investable assets; and (4) a liquid performing credit business managing approximately $8 billion.'}

