strategy_description:
EnSphere's Investment Fund primarily focuses on opportunities on Japan Rates and FX. Japan rates market is local and niche. Experience and deep understanding of JGB market are required to consistently generate alpha. Advantages of EnSphere's investments come from:
a. A unique set of knowledge and experience about pre-1999 Japan’s leading players, funding dynamics, policies. Sufficient precepts to discern practical policy implications vs. what is shown on headlines; 
b. Theoretical and applied expertise in macro cross-asset approaches. This provides the means to weigh how Japan’s interest rates, cross-currency, FX and derivatives tie into other global risk factors, including the intricacies and anomalies of the present market;
c. Advanced research toolkits, that includes proprietary models capitalizing on recent technologies such as statistical and machine learning techniques.

EnSphere believes bond and rates derivatives pricing theory finds its application in markets where organic liquidity and price formation exists. These frameworks do not stem from emotions or observing a narrow set of data points. Rather, when the nature of efficient markets regains traction, a scientific and mathematical approach suits naturally. The investment fund will capture the relevant rates and FX opportunities via a number of sub-strategies which ultimately compliment each other to form an absolute return profile.

management_company:
{'name': 'Axebrook Capital LLP', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.5159612, 'lon': -0.1439851}, 'description': 'Axebrook Capital LLP ("Axebrook") is a London-based partnership established by founder and CIO Jack Land.  Axebrook is authorised and regulated by the Financial Conduct Authority to act as an Alternative Investment Fund Manager.  

Prior to Axebrook, Jack was at York Capital Management ("York"), where since July 2020 he was lead portfolio manager for the Axebrook Credit Alpha Fund ("ACA" or the "Fund", formerly known as the York Global Credit Income Fund).  With effect from 1 February 2022, Axebrook replaced York as investment manager of the Fund.  The master and feeder fund vehicles remain unchanged and existing investors fully consented to the spinoff. Day 1 capital was in excess of $100 million, with substantial support via a seeding arrangement with York affiliated investors. 

The Axebrook team was built up during 2021 and brings with it significant industry experience.'}

{'name': 'Chenavari Financial Group Ltd', 'city': 'London', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 51.4970873, 'lon': -0.1395648}, 'description': "Chenavari is an established, credit-focused asset manager with a core expertise in European markets. With expertise across the liquidity spectrum of credit, Chenavari aims to profit from idiosyncrasies and inefficiencies within credit markets, which are due to macro (such as banks' deleveraging, monetary policies, etc.) as well as technical factors. The Firm concentrates its investment activity on fundamental strategies that may offer attractive risk-reward profiles on a relative value basis with low market correlation and low beta to broad credit markets.

Chenavari’s investment strategies can be segmented across three groups: 

•	Liquid strategies, including investments in single name corporates, European financials, credit indices, asset-backed securities, across both cash and derivative markets;
•	Private Credit strategies, such as portfolio acquisitions of primarily performing loans; risk sharing/significant risk transfer, asset-based lending, and specialty finance (new loan origination) in consumer finance, receivables and leasing; and
•	CLO management, including investment in senior secured loans and revolving credit facilities through European collateralised loan obligation structures."}

