•	CLO management, including investment in senior secured loans and revolving credit facilities through European collateralised loan obligation structures."}

{'name': 'Contingency Capital', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United Kingdom', 'location': {'lat': 40.7590245, 'lon': -73.97168359999999}, 'description': 'Contingency Capital invests in legal assets: we finance illiquid assets where the primary driver for unlocking the asset’s value is related to a legal, tax, or regulatory process. This includes loans to law firms, buying and financing claims, financing portfolios of litigation claims, and investing in other special situations assets that are uncorrelated to the public equity and debt markets. Unlike other litigation funders, we look at a broader scope of investments and take a credit-oriented approach. We try to structure our investments to have seniority, floating interest rates, and downside and duration protection.

Our first fund, Contingency Capital Fund I launched in June 2021 and had its final close in December 2022. It is approximately 60% deployed and we expect to be fully invested during the second half of 2024. The investments in Fund I have generated a cash-on cash return of 13% over their life and are generally uncorrelated to the broader credit and equity markets. We are targeting a first close for Fund II in the second quarter of 2024.

The fund manager, Contingency Capital LLC, was founded by Brandon Baer, who has over 20 years of experience investing in legal assets at D. E. Shaw and Fortress before founding Contingency Capital in late 2020. In addition to Fund I, Contingency Capital manages a fund of one targeting both high and lower yield opportunities of shorter duration. As of September 30, 2023, Contingency Capital has approximately $690 million of AUM. The Contingency Capital team has seven people, the majority of whom are women, and is supported by over 30 employees at TFG Asset Management.'}

{'name': 'Paradigm BioCapital Advisors LP', 'city': 'New York', 'country': 'United States of America', 'location': {'lat': 40.7541811, 'lon': -73.9713866}, 'description': 'Paradigm BioCapital manages an equity long/short hedge fund focused on the innovative biotechnology subsector of healthcare.

We believe that the most attractive investments deliver transformative benefits to patients and redefine the treatment paradigm for physicians. Paradigm’s investment strategy focuses on identifying such opportunities at the earliest proof of concept where the balance of reward and risk is at its apex. Identifying such opportunities requires not only rigorous scientific and medical analysis, but also a deep and nuanced understanding of the current treatment landscape and gaps in the standards of care. 

We bring decades of experience in biotech investing and medicine together with a proven, clearly defined strategy to deliver superior returns for our investors'}

